00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:09,473
when you paint your roof,

435
00:17:09,473 --> 00:17:11,730
white people are familiar with that, yeah?

436
00:17:11,730 --> 00:17:14,280
So that's one solution for extreme heat.

437
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:17,167
And if you can give cities the ability to understand,

438
00:17:17,167 --> 00:17:19,770
"What is my cool roof coverage at a city level?"

439
00:17:19,770 --> 00:17:21,270
That allows 'em to understand

440
00:17:21,270 --> 00:17:23,250
what policy tools they have in mind.

441
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:25,590
Also, tree canopy cover is another lever

442
00:17:25,590 --> 00:17:28,410
that cities can use to be able to combat heat.

443
00:17:28,410 --> 00:17:31,590
And so we provide at the census level data

444
00:17:31,590 --> 00:17:33,510
so that cities can understand

445
00:17:33,510 --> 00:17:35,340
